'''Acheron''' (Asheron) is a language in the [[Talodi languages|Talodi]] family spoken in [[South Kordofan]], [[Sudan]].

Acheron derives from the Arabic word {{IPA|aɟɟur-uun}}{{sic}} which means "innocent people",{{sfn|Norton|2013|p=195}} it was later "indigenised as {{IPA|/acʊrʊn/}}"<ref>{{harvnb|Stevenson|1956|p=102}}, quoted in {{harvnb|Norton|2013|p=195}}</ref> and turned into {{IPA|/aʃərɔn/}}. The autoethonym in Acheron is {{IPA|/wɑ-rəmɛ/}} for the people and {{IPA|/ɡə-rəmɛ/}} for the language.{{sfn|Norton|2013|p=195}}

The number of active speakers is estimated to be 9,800.{{sfn|Norton|2013|p=195}} This number includes the community members and "diaspora speakers" in other Sudanese towns and abroad.{{sfn|Norton|2013|p=195}}

